task: raft-leftovers
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/raft-leftovers
worktree: ../okay-wt-left

why: persist-raft's box has three bullets left after stages 0-2c
  and pre-vote, each filed "if the sim shows it mattering" or "as a
  contract question". Decide them the way the rest were decided —
  by a number from the simulator or by the contract — so the box
  closes on evidence, not on fatigue.

what: (1) the joiner's catch-up phase (thesis §4.2.1): measure in
  the membership sweep how long a sixth node takes from addNode to
  being current with the leader, and how many entries the cluster
  committed meanwhile — if a joiner is current within a round, a
  non-voting phase buys nothing at these sizes; (2) chunked
  InstallSnapshot: the wire frame is [len:int32][CBOR], one message
  up to 2 GB, so chunking is flow control, not correctness — stated
  with the frame limit; (3) the commit-wait as an Ack level: Topic's
  append returns the record's OFFSET, which exists only once applied,
  i.e. committed — every Ack level must wait for the commit, and the
  timeout stays the only honest knob. Boards: the persist-raft box.
